{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_kind": "profiles",
  "_README": "Column-role aliases for instrument exports — Roadmap P4. This is DATA, not code: when someone in the group meets an export whose header this does not recognise, they add the alias here and commit, and every future import understands it. Aliases are matched case-insensitively after normalising separators, so 'Voltage_V', 'voltage (V)' and 'VOLTAGE/V' all match 'voltage'. Detection is always shown to the user as a proposal to confirm — it is never applied silently, because a current column read as a voltage column produces a plot that looks entirely reasonable and is nonsense.",
  "_note_on_units": "Each role lists the units its column may carry, with the factor that converts to SI. A header like 'I/mA' or 'Current (A)' sets the unit automatically; where it does not, the user picks. This is the same unit engine the formula library uses, and for the same reason — mA read as A is a factor of a thousand and produces no error anywhere.",
